From: Dynamic Devices Ltd <support@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] tas2555: program coherent DEV ROM1 PLL and DAC clocks

Use TI's ROM1 clock tree for the Screen's 12.288 MHz MCLK. PLL/DSP
is 86.016 MHz (J=7); N=7 and MDAC=4 give a 3.072 MHz DAC clock,
64 times the 48 kHz sample rate. The former BCLK/PLL-off startup
produced moving n*1500 +/- input sampling images during playback.

Program the complete block while powered down on every DEV startup:
normal shutdown switches PLL input back to the internal oscillator.
Keep ROM coefficients, data pins, gain, boost/I-V disable and mute
lifecycle unchanged. Firmware-backed startup is untouched.

Reference: TI DINtoDOUTTestROM1.txt in E2E thread 1192205.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific development ROM1 mode]
Assisted-by: Briar
---
 tas2555-core.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tas2555-core.c b/tas2555-core.c
--- a/tas2555-core.c
+++ b/tas2555-core.c
@@ -139,9 +139,24 @@
-static unsigned int p_tas2555_rom1_dev_startup_data[] = {
-	TAS2555_CLK_ERR_CTRL1, 0x00,
-	TAS2555_MAIN_CLKIN_REG, 0x00,
-	TAS2555_POWER_CTRL2_REG, 0x80,
-	TAS2555_POWER_CTRL1_REG, 0xB8,
-	TAS2555_UDELAY, 2000,
-	TAS2555_CLK_ERR_CTRL1, 0x02,
-	0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF
-};
+static unsigned int p_tas2555_rom1_dev_startup_data[] = {
+	TAS2555_CLK_ERR_CTRL1, 0x00,
+	TAS2555_POWER_CTRL1_REG, 0x00,
+	TAS2555_MAIN_CLKIN_REG, 0x0F,
+	TAS2555_PLL_CLKIN_REG, 0x0D,
+	TAS2555_PLL_P_VAL_REG, 0x01,
+	TAS2555_PLL_J_VAL_REG, 0x07,
+	TAS2555_PLL_D_VAL_MSB_REG, 0x00,
+	TAS2555_PLL_D_VAL_LSB_REG, 0x00,
+	TAS2555_PLL_N_VAL_REG, 0x07,
+	TAS2555_REG(100, 0, 34), 0x08,
+	TAS2555_REG(100, 0, 2), 0x10,
+	TAS2555_DAC_MADC_VAL_REG, 0x04,
+	TAS2555_DAC_INTERPOL_REG, 0x08,
+	TAS2555_RAMP_CLK_DIV_MSB_REG, 0x00,
+	TAS2555_RAMP_CLK_DIV_LSB_REG, 0x20,
+	TAS2555_CLK_MISC_REG, 0x20,
+	TAS2555_ISENSE_DIV_REG, 0x40,
+	TAS2555_POWER_CTRL2_REG, 0x80,
+	TAS2555_POWER_CTRL1_REG, 0xF8,
+	TAS2555_UDELAY, 2000,
+	TAS2555_CLK_ERR_CTRL1, 0x0B,
+	0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF
+};
